# Godot Environment Variables
--env GODOT_HEADLESS=true
--env DISPLAY=:99

# Runner image: pin the slim act image (~1.6GB). act's default
# (catthehacker/ubuntu:full-latest, ~4GB) stalls pulling on slow links (#858).
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Container architecture
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Docker container options for Godot (volumes and shm-size)
--container-options --volume=/home/runner/.local/share/godot:/root/.local/share/godot
--container-options --volume=/home/runner/.config/godot:/root/.config/godot
--container-options --shm-size=2gb

# NOTE: --pull=false was removed in #858. It existed only to reuse a locally
# built `armored-archer/nakama-postgres:3.21.1` image that was never published
# to any registry. CI services now use standard public images
# (postgres:14-alpine / postgres:15-alpine / heroiclabs/nakama), so act should
# pull them normally — keeping --pull=false broke fresh machines that had not
# pre-pulled those images.

# Parallel act runs (issue #858):
# - act job containers run on the host network and reach service containers
#   via their published host ports (localhost:<host-port>); service DNS names
#   do NOT resolve.
# - Every DB-dependent CI job now publishes a UNIQUE host port — ci.yml
#   backend-test 5432, sonarcloud 5434, coverage-threshold.yml 5435,
#   test.yml backend-tests 5436, ci.yml schema-validation 5437 — none of which
#   collide with the local dev stack (postgres 5433, nakama 7349-7351), so
#   different jobs can run in parallel act processes.
# - The SAME job still cannot run in two act processes at once: act derives
#   job container names from workflow+job, and both invocations would bind the
#   same fixed host port. Run same-job invocations sequentially; they also
#   share ~/.cache/act (action cache races otherwise).
#
# Host memory (issue #993):
# - act Node-job containers plus concurrent NATIVE ./scripts/local-godot-tests.sh
#   suites on the same host can exhaust host RAM and OOM-kill jobs — act reports
#   exitcode '137' with no error output. Run the act matrix and native Godot
#   suites sequentially, never concurrently.
# - scripts/ci-local.sh warns/waits before each act job when available memory
#   is low (ACT_MIN_FREE_MB, default 2048; ACT_MEM_WAIT_SECS, default 60).
#
# For optimized local CI (sequential/parallel job orchestration):
#   - make ci (sequential)
#   - make ci-parallel (fastest)
#   - ./scripts/ci-local.sh --help (for options)
